1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,100
Last time we met the abacus.

2
00:00:02,620 --> 00:00:04,980
Today we're going to make numbers with it.

3
00:00:05,340 --> 00:00:08,620
Every number from zero all the way to nine.

4
00:00:08,620 --> 00:00:11,240
And we only need one rod.

5
00:00:11,920 --> 00:00:14,100
Let's start with nothing at all.

6
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:15,340
Zero.

7
00:00:16,320 --> 00:00:19,440
Zero means no beads are touching the beam.

8
00:00:20,320 --> 00:00:23,960
Push them all away, the rod says zero.

9
00:00:25,220 --> 00:00:28,040
Now push one lower bead up to the beam.

10
00:00:28,040 --> 00:00:29,960
That is one.

11
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:32,000
Push one more.

12
00:00:32,380 --> 00:00:34,700
One, two.

13
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:36,140
That is two.

14
00:00:36,540 --> 00:00:38,360
One more again.

15
00:00:39,140 --> 00:00:42,960
One, two, three.

16
00:00:43,420 --> 00:00:44,620
That is three.

17
00:00:45,160 --> 00:00:46,400
One more.

18
00:00:46,960 --> 00:00:52,840
One, two, three, four.

19
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:54,320
That is four.

20
00:00:55,220 --> 00:00:57,060
Now let's make five.

21
00:00:57,620 --> 00:00:59,800
Push another lower bead up.

22
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:02,620
Oh, there aren't any left.

23
00:01:03,320 --> 00:01:06,380
Four is as high as the lower beads can go.

24
00:01:07,120 --> 00:01:08,740
So how do we make five?

25
00:01:09,860 --> 00:01:11,140
Look above the beam.

26
00:01:11,700 --> 00:01:12,500
The upper bead.

27
00:01:13,060 --> 00:01:15,640
It has been waiting there the whole time.

28
00:01:16,360 --> 00:01:18,640
Send the lower beads back down.

29
00:01:19,640 --> 00:01:22,640
Now bring the upper bead down with your index finger.

30
00:01:23,640 --> 00:01:27,720
One upper bead, the rod says five.

31
00:01:28,100 --> 00:01:32,640
That one little bead is worth five all by itself.

32
00:01:33,580 --> 00:01:35,580
Now five is easy to build on.

33
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:39,680
Five and one lower bead, that's six.

34
00:01:40,480 --> 00:01:43,720
Five and two lower beads, seven.

35
00:01:44,260 --> 00:01:47,300
Five and three, eight.

36
00:01:47,900 --> 00:01:50,640
Five and four, nine.

37
00:01:50,640 --> 00:01:55,140
Nine is the biggest number one rod can show.

38
00:01:55,480 --> 00:01:58,400
Reading a rod is always the same.

39
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:01,440
First, is the upper bead down?

40
00:02:01,940 --> 00:02:04,140
If it is, that's five.

41
00:02:05,400 --> 00:02:07,820
Then count the lower beads touching the beam.

42
00:02:08,520 --> 00:02:11,100
Add them together, that's your number.

43
00:02:12,280 --> 00:02:12,940
Your turn.

44
00:02:13,260 --> 00:02:15,160
What number is this rod showing?

45
00:02:17,520 --> 00:02:18,580
It's three.

46
00:02:18,980 --> 00:02:22,440
Three lower beads are touching the beam.

47
00:02:23,080 --> 00:02:24,620
The upper bead is still up.

48
00:02:25,160 --> 00:02:26,100
Nice work.

49
00:02:26,760 --> 00:02:31,420
Now it's your turn, make every number from zero to nine.

50
00:02:32,460 --> 00:02:36,080
If you liked this, tap like and subscribe for more.

51
00:02:36,560 --> 00:02:40,180
Search for abacus kids on the Apple App Store or Google Play.

52
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:41,880
Download it free.

53
00:02:41,880 --> 00:02:47,460
See you in the next video, where we'll add two numbers together on the abacus.
